      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "\"Proponents paint UBI as a shiny promise of a better tomorrow, but the reality is a path to economic stagnation and dependency. UBI is not a foundation for justice; it is a costly trap that discourages work, undermining the very industriousness that builds a strong society. Instead of empowering citizens, it risks creating a large class dependent on the state, draining our economy without delivering genuine opportunity. We must choose productive investment over the illusion of universal handouts.\"",
      "source": "target",
